Lululemon built an $11 billion brand selling the idea of wellness, sustainability, and healthy living. Texas AG 
@KenPaxtonTX
 wants to know if the clothes themselves tell a different story. Paxton issued a Civil Investigative Demand to Lululemon on April 13, launching a formal probe into whether the company's activewear contains PFAS, the synthetic compounds known as forever chemicals because they do not break down in the human body or the environment. PFAS have been linked to endocrine disruption, infertility, and cancer. Independent lab testing has raised questions about what is actually in the fabric, and where it concentrates. Lululemon says it phased PFAS out in 2023 and is cooperating with the investigation. The full article has the details. Get all of the details in this piece by 
@smiddendorp22
 linked below.

This is concerning. As a loyal 
@lululemon
 customer for years, it’s worrying that they only phased out PFAS in 2023. Lululemon should promptly contact their customers. https://smh.com.au/business/consumer-affairs/lululemon-s-athletic-wear-faces-probe-into-forever-chemicals-20260414-p5znn9.html…

